{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793726044,"nonce":"2L5mxwE6UwbDW03MR//IJ6Q149M=","message":"Decided 2026-11-03 (owner): build it, do not refuse (pre-1.0). Schedules stay in the YAML; default branch only.\n\nSyntax: `on: cron: { schedule: \"0 2 * * *\" }` (string or list), UTC only, `when:` still applies. Check refuses a schedule that does not parse or fires more than once a minute.\n\nIndex: table `pipeline_schedules` keyed by (repo, pipeline path, schedule): source commit, delivered_at, next_fire_at. Holds only the cron triggers of the compiled IR, not the IR.\n- A push to the default branch replaces the repo's rows in one transaction from the compile pass that already runs; other branches never write. A row is not overwritten by an older delivery.\n- A push whose pipeline fails to compile keeps that pipeline's last good rows (each fire then leaves a refused Run).\n- Binding a repo fills its rows; unbinding drops them. Daily re-read of the default branch: later, tracked here.\n\nFiring: the ADR-0077 leader's tick selects rows with next_fire_at \u003c= now and claims each with a CAS on next_fire_at inside its term-fenced transaction, then calls dispatch_run at the default branch head. next_fire_at is computed from now, so missed slots fire once. Fire-time check: the recompiled IR must still declare that schedule, else the row is deleted and no Run is made. A refused dispatch is a refused Run, not a retry.\n\nEvent: cron carries repo, ref refs/heads/\u003cdefault\u003e, commit and schedule; allowed_refs treats it as a push to the default branch (replaces \"a cron run has no symbolic ref\"). No actor; Headline = schedule (ADR-0057).\n\nDependency: one cron-expression parser crate (reason in the PR).\n\nWorst case accepted by the owner: a fire missed or late until the next push or re-read; refused-Run noise while the default branch does not compile. Never a double fire or a Run with wrong content.\n\nPRs: (1) syntax + event + index written on push; (2) tick, claim, fire-time check. Tests: slot maths with a fake clock; push replaces rows and a removed trigger stops; two replicas fire one Run per slot (PG); missed slots fire once; one kind fire. Docs: pipeline-syntax.mdx, index.mdx \"Missing\".","files":null}]}